Reconstruction Models

DUSt3R (Dense Unconstrained Stereo 3D Reconstruction) — Vision Transformer (ViT-Large, 24 layers) that takes two frames and predicts 3D pointmaps directly without feature matching
MonST3R (Motion and Structure in 3D) — extends DUSt3R with optical flow input and motion masks to handle dynamic scenes (moving cars)

Optimisation / Alignment

PointCloudOptimizer — DUSt3R's global alignment module; minimises a confidence-weighted energy function using Adam optimiser with cosine learning rate decay
Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) initialisation — initialises the global alignment by processing highest-confidence frame pairs first

Pose Estimation / Stitching

Umeyama Similarity Transform — SVD-based closed-form solver for scale + rotation + translation between chunks
SE(3) Rigid Transform Stitching — rigid pose composition using 4×4 homogeneous matrices to weld chunks together
PnP-RANSAC (solvePnPRansac) — OpenCV's internal pose initialisation used inside DUSt3R's chunk alignment

Supporting Methods

RAFT (Recurrent All-Pairs Field Transforms) — optical flow network used by MonST3R to estimate pixel motion between frames
Voxel Downsampling — Open3D spatial downsampling to remove duplicate points from the merged cloud
Bilinear Interpolation — used in ffmpeg resize step

Tools / Frameworks (not models but worth listing)

PyTorch, Open3D, ffmpeg, OpenCV, NumPy
